OVERVIEW: View DICOM images directly in the terminal

Display DICOM images using ASCII art, ANSI colors, or terminal graphics
protocols (iTerm2, Kitty, Sixel) for quick image inspection and triage.
All registered codecs (J2K, HTJ2K, JPEG-LS, RLE …) are used automatically.

Examples:
  dicom-viewer scan.dcm
  dicom-viewer scan.dcm --mode ascii --quality high
  dicom-viewer scan.dcm --mode ansi --color 24bit
  dicom-viewer ct.dcm --window-center -600 --window-width 1500
  dicom-viewer scan.dcm --show-info
  dicom-viewer series/*.dcm --thumbnail
  dicom-viewer j2k.dcm --reduce 2            # 1/4 resolution preview
  dicom-viewer ct.dcm --roi 100,50,256,256   # crop region x,y,w,h
  dicom-viewer volume.dcm --volume           # multi-frame / JP3D volume
  dicom-viewer --jpip "http://server/wado?..." # stream via JPIP

USAGE: dicom-viewer [<options>] <file-paths> ...

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-paths>            Path(s) to DICOM file(s)

OPTIONS:
  -m, --mode <mode>       Display mode: ascii, ansi, iterm2, kitty, sixel
                          (values: ascii, ansi, iterm2, kitty, sixel; default:
                          ascii)
  --quality <quality>     ASCII art quality: low, high (default: high) (values:
                          low, high; default: high)
  --color <color>         ANSI color depth: 256, 24bit (default: 24bit)
                          (values: 256, 24bit; default: 24bit)
  --window-center <window-center>
                          Window Center (level) for display, in Modality LUT
                          output units (e.g. HU)
  --window-width <window-width>
                          Window Width for display (>= 1 for LINEAR, > 0 for
                          LINEAR_EXACT and SIGMOID; PS3.3 C.11.2.1.2.1)
  --voi-lut-function <voi-lut-function>
                          VOI LUT Function (0028,1056) to apply the window
                          with: LINEAR, LINEAR_EXACT, SIGMOID (default: the
                          file's value, else LINEAR)
  --frame <frame>         Deprecated: 0-based index; use --frame-number (index
                          0 is Frame number 1)
  --frame-number <frame-number>
                          Frame number to display, 1-based (PS3.3 Table 10-3:
                          the first Frame is Frame number 1); default 1
  --width <width>         Output width in characters
  --height <height>       Output height in characters
  --invert                Invert pixel values
  --show-info             Show patient and study information overlay
  --show-overlay          Draw overlay planes (60xx, PS3.3 C.9.2) and show a
                          frame/size status line
  --thumbnail             Display as thumbnail grid (for multiple files or
                          frames)
  --size <size>           Thumbnail grid size as WxH (e.g., 80x40)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --reduce <reduce>       Resolution reduce factor n: decode at 1/2^n spatial
                          resolution (0 = full). (default: 0)
  --roi <roi>             Region of interest as "x,y,width,height" (pixel
                          coordinates, 0-based).
  --volume                Volume / multi-frame mode: display all frames as a
                          thumbnail filmstrip.
  --jpip <jpip>           Fetch and display image from a JPIP server URL
                          (currently unavailable: upstream JPIP retrieval is
                          unimplemented — see RESEARCH_ADOPTION_PLAN.md F1).
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

